'[info]'
Title = "Last Stand";
briefing = "Last Stand
Date: October 4, 1993 - 0600 hours
Location:  Mogadishu, Somalia 

Situation:
Enemy mortars are pinning down your team. You must get around behind their position, and take them out with a satchel charge. Once they are clear, your team will be able to make their way back to base.
";
briefing2 = "<cFC8932>Last Stand<-co>
FRAGO: 4 TFR  REF: OPORD 10-93 TFR Date Time: 040600 October 93 

1. <ucFC8932>Situation<-uco> 
Habr Gedir forces have overrun the 2nd crash site. All crew are captured or killed. We are recalling all units back to base. Aerial recon shows enemy mortar emplacements near your location that will have to be eliminated to clear your exfil.

      <cFC8932>Weather:<-co>  Hazy, dim light, hot.
      <cFC8932>Terrain:<-co>  Urban - City center.
      <cFC8932>Enemy:<-co>  Estimated 500 Habr Gedir militia equipped with small arms, grenades and RPG’s. Technicals w/ .50 caliber mounted weapons.
      <cFC8932>Friendly:<-co>  None

2. <ucFC8932>Mission<-uco> 
      <cFC8932>Who:<-co> Delta 5
      <cFC8932>What:<-co> Eliminate mortars, get team out of Mogadishu’s center.
      <cFC8932>When:<-co> Immediately.

3. <ucFC8932>Execution<-uco>
      <cFC8932>Commanders Intent:<-co>  Return team safely to base.
      <cFC8932>Concept of Operation:<-co>  Aerial recon shows mortars pinning down your team. If you can circle behind it and plant a satchel, your team can get out safely. A lot is riding on this, so proceed cautiously, and methodically eliminate opposing forces.
      <cFC8932>Coordinating instructions: <-co> 

4. <ucFC8932>Service and Support<-uco>
      <cFC8932>Basic Load:<-co>  CAR15/M203, Colt .45, Satchel Charges

5. <ucFC8932>Command and signal<-uco>
	Task Force chain of command in effect.  Command will coordinate from recon helo. Hand and arm signals TACSOP, with higher via FM primary and SATCOM alternate.  Standard unit CEOI

";

